.\" kpxcctl.1 — Man page for the KeePassXC Daemon CLI client
.TH KPXCTL 1 "2026-05-18" "kpxcd" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
kpxcctl \- command-line client for the KeePassXC daemon

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kpxcctl
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGUMENTS\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kpxcctl
is the command-line interface to \fBkpxcd\fR(8), the KeePassXC headless daemon.
It communicates with the daemon over the D-Bus session bus to manage databases,
retrieve entries, and perform SSH and passkey operations.

All operations require that \fBkpxcd\fR is running and reachable on the D-Bus
session bus.

.SH COMMANDS
.SS unlock
Unlock a KeePass database.

.nf
.B kpxcctl unlock <path>
.fi

Prompts for the database password on stdin. The database is then held in
memory by the daemon until explicitly locked or until the idle timeout expires.

.SS lock
Lock a database or all databases.

.nf
.B kpxcctl lock [uuid|all]
.fi

If no argument or \fBall\fR is given, all unlocked databases are locked.
If a UUID is given, only that database is locked. Decrypted data is wiped
from memory using secure zeroing.

.SS list
List all known databases and their lock status.

.nf
.B kpxcctl list [--json]
.fi

Displays a table of UUID, name, lock status, and path. Use \fB\-\-json\fR
for machine-readable output.

.SS get
Retrieve fields for a specific entry.

.nf
.B kpxcctl get <uuid> <entry-path>
.fi

The entry path is a slash-separated path from the root group, e.g.,
\fI/General/example.com\fR. Displays title, username, password, URL, and
current TOTP code (if configured). Password retrieval may require Polkit
authorization.

.SS ssh
Manage SSH keys stored in KeePass databases and served by the agent.

.TP
.B kpxcctl ssh list [uuid]
List SSH keys loaded in the agent. Optionally filter by database UUID.

.TP
.B kpxcctl ssh add <uuid> <entry-path>
Add an SSH key from the specified database entry to the agent.

.TP
.B kpxcctl ssh remove <fingerprint>
Remove an SSH key from the agent by its SHA256 fingerprint.

.TP
.B kpxcctl ssh scan [uuid]
Scan unlocked database(s) for entries containing SSH keys.
Shows entry UUID, title, key type, and fingerprint.

.TP
.B kpxcctl ssh show <fingerprint>
Show metadata for a loaded SSH key.

.TP
.B kpxcctl ssh generate <uuid> <entry-path> [\-\-type rsa|ed25519|ecdsa] [\-\-bits N] [\-\-comment text]
Generate a new SSH key pair, store the private key as an attachment in the
specified entry, and set KeeAgent metadata. The public key is not stored
separately; it can be derived from the private key attachment.

.TP
.B kpxcctl ssh import <uuid> <entry-path> <file> [\-\-passphrase] [\-\-delete-after]
Import an existing SSH private key into the database. The key file is
read, parsed, attached to the entry, and KeeAgent metadata is set.
With \fB\-\-delete-after\fR, the source file is removed after successful import.

.TP
.B kpxcctl ssh export <fingerprint> <file>
Export a loaded SSH private key to a file with mode 0600.
Warning: this writes unencrypted private key material to disk.

.TP
.B kpxcctl ssh test-sign <fingerprint>
Sign a test challenge with the specified loaded key to verify it works.

.TP
.B kpxcctl ssh diag
Print SSH agent diagnostics: mode, socket path, and loaded key summary.

.SS passkey
Manage FIDO2 / WebAuthn passkeys.

.TP
.B kpxcctl passkey create <uuid> <rpID> <username>
Create a new passkey credential in the specified database. The relying
party ID (e.g., \fIgithub.com\fR) and username are required.

.TP
.B kpxcctl passkey assert <rpID> <credentialID>
Authenticate with an existing passkey. The relying party ID and the
base64url-encoded credential ID are required.

.SS ping
Check whether the daemon is running and responsive.

.nf
.B kpxcctl ping
.fi

Prints \fIpong\fR if the daemon is alive. Exits with an error otherwise.

.SS help
Print usage information.

.SH OPTIONS
.B kpxcctl
does not accept global options. Each command may have its own flags (e.g.,
\fB\-\-json\fR for \fBlist\fR). Use \fBkpxcctl help\fR for command-specific
help.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS
D-Bus session bus address. If not set, the default session bus is used.
\fBkpxcctl\fR must be able to reach the same session bus as \fBkpxcd\fR.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B Unlock a database:
.nf
    kpxcctl unlock ~/Passwords.kdbx
.fi

.TP
.B Lock all databases:
.nf
    kpxcctl lock all
.fi

.TP
.B List databases in JSON format:
.nf
    kpxcctl list --json
.fi

.TP
.B Retrieve an entry:
.nf
    kpxcctl get abc123 /General/github.com
.fi

.TP
.B List SSH keys:
.nf
    kpxcctl ssh list
.fi

.TP
.B Check daemon status:
.nf
    kpxcctl ping
.fi

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kpxcd (8),
.BR kpxcd.toml (5),
.BR ssh-agent (1),
.BR dbus-daemon (1)
